      <div class="remember">
        <p class="note-label">Key takeaways</p>
        <ol>
          <li><code>=</code> stores: work out the right side, then store it in the variable on the left.</li>
          <li>Conditions choose a path (<code>else if</code> for more cases; <code>&amp;&amp;</code> = both, <code>||</code> = at least one, <code>!</code> = not). Loops repeat: <code>for</code> for a known number of rounds, <code>while</code> as long as a check is true. Methods package one task with inputs and an output.</li>
          <li>Array indexes start at 0, so <code>arr[2]</code> is the third value. <code>new int[5]</code> makes 5 slots, and <code>length</code> counts them.</li>
          <li>A complete program is a class with a <code>main</code> method. Java always starts at <code>main</code>.</li>
          <li>A trace table shows how each variable changes, one step at a time.</li>
          <li>Compile-time (syntax) errors stop the program before it runs, runtime errors crash it partway, and logic errors give wrong answers.</li>
        </ol>
